{
 "id": "301-49",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "So, if you have any particular preferences or traditions you'd like us to incorporate for your special day, just let HR know.",
  "Consistency is key, and we want to ensure that our code is readable and maintainable.",
  "One of the conventions we follow is to always include a single digit in our function names.",
  "Well, it's mainly for consistency and to avoid potential naming conflicts.",
  "By including a digit, we ensure that our function names are unique and descriptive.",
  "It also helps when we have multiple functions that serve similar purposes but with slight variations.",
  "Just remember to keep your code well-documented and follow our style guide, which you can find on our internal wiki.",
  "Remote work has become an essential part of our industry, especially after the pandemic.",
  "When we're not physically in the same space, it can be harder to stay aligned and ensure everyone is on the same page.",
  "This might mean scheduling regular check-ins with your team, providing clear and detailed updates, and being responsive to queries.",
  "Embracing remote work fully means recognizing and leveraging these unique advantages.",
  "It's also important to stay adaptable and resilient \u2013 remote work policies and practices might continue to evolve, so being open to change and quick to adjust is key.",
  "Finding that balance is key, and it's a continuous process.",
  "Remember, it's important to be efficient and practical in our work, especially in a fast-paced environment like SYNERGY.",
  "From now on, I need you always to include assert statements in your methods.",
  "Assert statements are vital for validating assumptions and catching errors early on.",
  "They act as a form of self-documentation, making the code more robust and easier to maintain.",
  "By including them, you're not only helping yourself but also futureproofing your code for your teammates."
 ],
 "admitted": 18,
 "relations_applied": 0,
